<title>CANADA: Hudson's Bay sees 1998 sales of C$3.5 bln.</title>
<headline>Hudson's Bay sees 1998 sales of C$3.5 bln.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hudson's Bay Co, Canada's largest department store retailer, has forecast sales of C$3.5 billion for the year ended January 31, 1998, chief executive Millard Barron told Reuters late on Monday.</p>
<p>Also, comparative stores sales will range for three to five percent for fiscal 1998, Barron said.</p>
<p>Sales for fiscal 1997, ending this month, were estimated at C$3.4 billion, Barron said earlier.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8109))</p>
</text>
